# Corrections

Cross-session memory. A conversation ends and takes its lessons with it; this file
does not.

**The rule:** every time the user has to correct the same thing twice, it gets one
dated line here. Not a paragraph, not a document — one line, in this shape:

```
- YYYY-MM-DD — <what went wrong> · <why it matters> · <what to do instead>
```

Load-bearing details:

- `CLAUDE.md` points at this file, so it is read at the start of every session. Keep
  it short enough that this is cheap: when it passes ~40 lines, promote the stable
  entries into the matching `.claude/rules/*.md` or into
  `.claude/skills/*/references/project-pitfalls.md` and delete them here.
- A line stays until it is wrong. Do not "clean up" old entries because they look
  obvious; they look obvious because they are written down.
- Entries about *how this project works* belong in `project.md`. Entries about *a
  mistake already paid for* belong here or in `project-pitfalls.md`. The difference:
  a correction has a date and a victim.
- Anything a script can enforce should become a hook or a `verify` step instead of a
  line here. A line here is the fallback for what only judgement catches.

## Entries

Seeded with the generic ones. Delete any that does not apply here, and add this
project's own below.

- 2026-09-16 — Commits carried `Co-Authored-By: Claude` / "Generated with Claude"
  trailers · the user does not want AI attribution in the public history, and prose
  asking for it is forgotten every session · it is enforced in
  `.claude/settings.json` (`includeCoAuthoredBy: false`, empty `attribution`); never
  write an attribution trailer by hand, and after committing check
  `git log -1 --format=%B` and amend if one slipped in.
- 2026-09-16 — Verification commands chained with `;` instead of `&&` · with `;` a
  failing typecheck is followed by a passing build and the run reads green, so broken
  code gets reported as done · chain every verification command with `&&`, and put
  the whole chain in the root `verify` script so it cannot be retyped wrong.
- 2026-09-16 — Edits failing with "string not found" right after a successful write ·
  the PostToolUse formatter rewrites the file (quotes, line breaks, trailing commas)
  so the anchor text no longer matches what was written · re-read the file before the
  next edit to it, and anchor edits on code that the formatter does not move
  (identifiers, not whitespace or punctuation).
- 2026-09-16 — Scripts written through shell heredocs arrived corrupted · backslashes
  and `$` are mangled by the shell layer before the file is written, and on Windows
  paths this silently breaks regexes and escapes · write files with the Write tool,
  never with `cat <<EOF`; use the shell for running things, not for authoring them.
- 2026-09-16 — A task was reported done after a refactor that was never asked for ·
  unrequested changes widen the diff, hide the real fix and make review expensive ·
  one fix per task, no drive-by refactors; after two failed attempts stop and ask
  instead of trying a third approach.

